The ffhn binary includes crates from crates.io and `htmlcut-core` plus its `htmlcut-*` companion
crates from the public HTMLCut v13.0.0 source tagged at
https://github.com/resoltico/HTMLCut. The root Cargo.toml identifies that immutable source, and
Cargo.lock records the exact resolved package graph. `cargo deny check advisories bans licenses sources` verifies the allowed license and source policy for that graph before release.

HTMLCut is MIT-licensed. Its parser stack includes the MPL-2.0 `cssparser`, `cssparser-macros`,
`dtoa-short`, and Servo-derived `htmlcut-selectors` crates. MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft; its
terms and covered sources remain available from their published upstream source packages. The
HTMLCut repository is intentionally an allowed Git source in `deny.toml`.

Other allowed dependency-license families are 0BSD, Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause,
CDLA-Permissive-2.0, ISC, MIT, Unicode-3.0, and Unlicense. The graph includes ISC-licensed `ring`
and related cryptographic components; Unicode and CDLA data components; and standard Rust ecosystem
crates under the listed permissive or dual licenses. The applicable notice and license text for a
dependency is the one published with that dependency's resolved source.

FFHN is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the upstream projects whose open-source
components are included in the binary.
